### Connecting and creating tags simultaneously

```ts
await prisma.post.update({
  where: { id: 1 },
  data: {
    title: "Prisma is awesome!",
    tags: { set: [{ id: 1 }, { id: 2 }], create: { name: "typescript" } },
  },
});
```

content.text:
Your schema uses an **implicit** many-to-many (no join model, just `Category[]`/`Brand[]` list fields on both sides). For implicit relations, Prisma removes the extra nesting level — you don't wrap in `{ category: { connect: ... } }`, you `connect`/`create` directly on the relation field.

Fix:
```ts
prisma.brand.create({
  data: {
    name, slug, userId: user, image: uploadedImage.secure_url,
    categories: {
      connect: [{ id: "ckzpl0del0014vcv2ctift2f1" }]
      // or create: { name: "New Category", slug: "...", userId: ... }
    }
  },
  include: { categories: true }
})
```

Source: `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v6/prisma-schema/data-model/relations/many-to-many-relations.mdx` § "Implicit many-to-many relations" and `apps/docs/content/docs/orm/v6/more/troubleshooting/many-to-many-relations.mdx` § "Connecting and creating tags simultaneously" (only used with implicit m-n, not the explicit join-table pattern with a nested `category: { connect }`).

